          "id": "s-26f00v",
          "visual": "v-26f00p",
          "number": "26 AUGUST 2026",
          "body": "### Nepal flash floods\n\nA massive flash flood swept through Nepal’s **Rasuwa district** and downstream areas after a sudden surge of water and debris entered the Bhote Koshi river system. It inundated settlements, washed away roads and bridges, and damaged hydropower projects.\n\nAs of August 31, authorities reported **over 900 deaths and nearly 4,500 missing**.",
          "align": "left",
          "state": {
            "center": [
              28.17,
              85.38
            ],
            "zoom": 7,
            "markers": [
              {
                "lat": 28.17,
                "lng": 85.38,
                "label": "Nepal, 2026"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "s-26f00w",
          "visual": "v-26f00p",
          "number": "26 DECEMBER 2004",
          "body": "### Indian Ocean tsunami\n\nA magnitude **9.1** earthquake off the coast of Sumatra triggered a tsunami that swept across every country bordering the Indian Ocean. Indonesia, Sri Lanka, India and Thailand were worst affected.\n\nAbout **228,000 people** were killed or left missing and presumed dead — one of the deadliest natural disasters in recorded history.",
          "align": "left",
          "state": {
            "center": [
              3.316,
              95.854
            ],
            "zoom": 5,
            "markers": [
              {
                "lat": 28.17,
                "lng": 85.38,
                "label": "Nepal, 2026"
              },
              {
                "lat": 3.316,
                "lng": 95.854,
                "label": "Indian Ocean, 2004"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "s-26f00x",
          "visual": "v-26f00q",
          "number": "",
          "body": "Aceh, weeks later. Whole settlements on the Sumatran coast were simply removed.",
          "align": "left",
          "state": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s-26f00y",
          "visual": "v-26f00p",
          "number": "26 DECEMBER 2003",
          "body": "### Bam earthquake\n\nA magnitude **6.6** earthquake destroyed much of the historic Iranian city of **Bam**. Thousands of buildings collapsed. Estimates of the toll varied, with figures of about **31,000** widely reported.",
          "align": "left",
          "state": {
            "center": [
              29.11,
              58.36
            ],
            "zoom": 7,
            "markers": [
              {
                "lat": 28.17,
                "lng": 85.38,
                "label": "Nepal, 2026"
              },
              {
                "lat": 3.316,
                "lng": 95.854,
                "label": "Indian Ocean, 2004"
              },
              {
                "lat": 29.11,
                "lng": 58.36,
                "label": "Bam, 2003"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "s-26f00z",
          "visual": "v-26f00r",
          "number": "",
          "body": "Arg-e Bam, the mud-brick citadel at the heart of the city. Much of it came down in the quake.",
          "align": "left",
          "state": {}
        },
        {
          "id": "s-26f010",
          "visual": "v-26f00p",
          "number": "26 JANUARY 2001",
          "body": "### Gujarat earthquake\n\nA powerful earthquake devastated large parts of Gujarat, particularly the **Kutch** region. More than **166,000 people were injured** and around **20,000 killed** — on Republic Day.",
          "align": "left",
          "state": {
            "center": [
              23.42,
              70.31
